                <p style="color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">
                    <strong>Reading the diagram:</strong> every red <strong>5V</strong> dot is the same power rail — connect them all together (a breadboard power rail is perfect for this). Every <strong>&#x23DA; ground symbol</strong> is the same ground rail — all grounds must connect together. With two servos running, feed that 5V rail from an <strong>external 5V supply</strong> if things get jittery, and always keep the supply's GND tied to the Arduino's GND.
